# My Clay Hub — AGENTS.md

## Source of truth
- `docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md` and `DECISIONS.md` define this app. Don't change a documented rule or add scope without asking
  Christie. Log new decisions at the bottom of `DECISIONS.md`, dated.
- Brand values come from `docs/my-clay-hub/DESIGN.md` and `docs/my-clay-hub/brand/`. The `design-reference/` mockups are
  for layout only.
- Staff screens are a `/staff` section of this app, signed into by exchanging the Tinker HQ login (`exchangeStaffSession`,
  checked live against `staffRoster`). Staff access is removed by unticking `my-clay-hub` in Manage Team, not by disabling
  the login (DECISIONS #31).
- Never reuse the retired Clay Hub Booking app's code or collections (`clayMembers`, `clayBookings`, `claySpots`,
  `clayBlockedSlots`, `claySettings`).

## Member data
- Membership Manager (`clayHub_members` in `tinker-hq-apps`) is the only source of member records. This app never
  writes back to it.
- The only copy is the `members/*` projection in this app's own project. It's written only by `ingestMemberUpdate`, and
  it holds the last 4 digits of the phone at most, never the full number. Clients never read `members/*`; members read only
  their own `memberProfiles/{memberId}` (an allowlist without the phone digits).

## Firebase: own project (`my-clay-hub`), not `tinker-hq-apps`
- The project exists (Sep 28, 2026; Firestore `nam5`) and its rules deny everything until Phase F. **Never put this
  app's collections or rules in `/Users/christiehubley/studio-hub/firestore.rules`.**
- This repo's `firestore.rules` and `storage.rules` only, deployed only through this repo's guard
  (`scripts/deploy-rules.sh --status` / `--diff` / `--approved <full sha>`) after "approved to change firebase <full
  sha>" for that exact commit — never studio-hub's guard or a `tinker-hq-apps` approval. Tests:
  `npm test` (unit, rules guard, functions guard, functions and rules suites; emulators only, project
  `demo-my-clay-hub`; the functions suite needs Node 22 and every codebase in `firebase.json` installed (today `core`) —
  `"$NODE22" /opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/lib/node_modules/npm/bin/npm-cli.js ci --prefix functions/<cb>` — and otherwise
  prints SKIPPED). A raw `firebase … deploy` is denied.
- Cloud Functions: HTTP and scheduled functions only, for now, in `functions/<codebase>/`, deployed only through
  `scripts/deploy-functions.sh` (`--status` / `--diff` / `--approved <full sha>`, each with `--codebase <cb>`; then
  `--attest` when the guard says an IAM reading is needed; recovery in `FUNCTIONS-ROLLBACK.md`) after the same phrase. Every function is declared in
  `functions/declarations.json` (runtime account and callers) and declares `invoker` in code — never grant `run.invoker`
  by hand; every HTTP response sets `x-tinker-reached` (scheduled functions excepted: the SDK writes their response —
  `FUNCTIONS-ROLLBACK.md` §9); no `.env*`, `functions.yaml`, symlinks or `node` dependency in a
  codebase; the canary (`core/canary`) is permanent. Deleting functions, secrets, runtime config and artifact settings
  have no guarded path: ask Christie.
- `updateDoc` for partial updates; strip empty fields; `await` critical writes; snapshot before bulk delete or import; a
  new collection gets a new rule in the same commit.

## Test requirements
- Data-write, rules or delete changes: write a failing emulator test first, then fix it, then go green.
- Time logic is tested for America/Denver, both DST changes, and Mon–Sun week boundaries.
- Dates, week keys and member status come only from `shared/denver-time.js` and `shared/derive-status.js` (no Firebase
  import; used by the app and the functions). Never `new Date('YYYY-MM-DD')`; never re-derive status elsewhere. Their tests
  (`tests/shared/`) must pass identically under TZ=UTC, America/Denver and Pacific/Auckland (`tests/unit/tz-matrix.test.js`).
- A "writes nothing" test always has a positive pair.

## Commit discipline
- Commit after each phase, not at the end of a session.
- Format: `type: what changed and why` (fix, feat, refactor, docs, chore).
- Never `--no-verify`.

## Planning
- Use `/planning-workflow` for any non-trivial change, one phase at a time.
- Plans live in `~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/<slug>.html` (foundation plan: `clayhub-members-foundation.html`).
- No execution without a reviewed plan for data-write or rules changes.
36-  <strong>Not in this plan:</strong> any screen, sign-in provider or <code>claimMembership</code> (Phase F); the Tinker HQ tile and the Manage Team <code>my-clay-hub</code> box (Phase F); "change email" in Membership Manager (B4, its own plan); <code>kioskLookup</code>; any write back to Membership Manager (never, D6).<br>
37-  <strong>Risk:</strong> <strong>HIGH.</strong> The first Cloud Functions ever in <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>, the project every staff app shares; real member personal data crossing projects for the first time; IAM changes in both projects, including one Google makes on its own (K13).<br>
38-  <strong>Size:</strong> roughly 2 weeks at the D-4 cadence (several review rounds per PR). Christie's hands-on time ≈ 6–10 h (decisions, Console/IAM steps, approvals, a 3-member spot check).<br>
39:  <strong>Status:</strong> <span class="status-tag ready">execution-ready: true</span> — v4.1, Oct 8, 2026, after four review rounds (round 4: Codex and Claude both "ready after fixes", 0 blocking; all fixes applied). Christie answered Q1–Q9 on Oct 8 (Q7 changed: removed members keep everything but email and phone digits). <strong>Marked execution-ready (all phases) by Christie, Oct 8.</strong> Next: E-pre (its PR review re-checks the Q7 change).
