# Clay Hub Membership Management — AGENTS.md

## Firebase Safety (non-negotiable)
- `updateDoc` for partial updates; `setDoc` only for intentional full overwrites
- Strip empty fields before writing; `await` all critical writes
- Snapshot before bulk delete/import
- New collection → new rule in `/Users/christiehubley/studio-hub/firestore.rules`, same commit
- Deploy rules: ONLY through `/Users/christiehubley/studio-hub/scripts/deploy-rules.sh --approved <full sha>`, after Christie says "approved to change firebase <full sha>"
  (`--status` prints the sentence). A raw `firebase … deploy` in any form is refused by the predeploy check in `firebase.json`

## Honest saves (B1, Sep 2026) — never confirm an unsaved change
- No confirmation text ("Saved!", "✓ …", "… completed", "… added") may be added to `app.js` without awaiting its save first.
- Pattern: `const before = snapshotOf(record)` → change → `if (!await saveMemberChanges(record)) return notSaved(what, [[record, before]])` → only then close the window and confirm. `notSaved` puts the record back (so trying again can't apply a change twice), redraws, and says "Not saved — try again"; the window stays open. Save buttons use `showSaveOutcome(btn, ok, idleText)`.
- Wrap user-triggered save handlers in `oneAtATime(...)` when repeating them would apply a change twice (e.g. record a pause twice). Simple field auto-saves (trade status) needn't be: the data layer queues saves of a record.
- Save through `saveOrUndo(record, before)` so a failed save undoes only its own change, inside the data layer's turn (`opts.onFail`).
- Two-document changes save the member first (a failure writes nothing), then the waitlist entry, and say so if the second fails.
- `saveMemberChanges` / `saveWaitlistMemberToFirestore` resolve true/false; every false is also reported on the red banner by the data layer.
- Background saves with no confirmation (load-time checks, action log, custom alerts, onboarding checklist auto-saves) rely on the banner.
- Out of scope: `clayHub_appData` saves (`saveAppDataToFirestore`) still don't report failures.

## Shelf Map storage split
- Shelf assignments for members → Firestore (`clayHub_members`)
- Write-in labels for non-members → localStorage only
- Do not migrate write-in labels to Firestore without Christie's explicit approval

## Test requirements
- Data-write / rules / delete changes: write a failing emulator test first, then fix, then green
- Rules test suite: `cd /Users/christiehubley/studio-hub && npm test` (must pass: check the printed count — don't hardcode a number, it drifts as tests are added)
- Emulator: `firebase emulators:start --only firestore` from `/Users/christiehubley/studio-hub/`

## Deployment
- Render auto-deploys on GitHub push — no manual deploy step needed
- Do NOT use `netlify deploy` for this app

## Commit discipline
- Commit after each phase, not at the end of a session
- Format: `type: what changed and why` (fix, feat, refactor, docs, chore)
- Never `--no-verify`

## Planning
- Use `/planning-workflow` for any non-trivial change
- Plans: `~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/<slug>.html`
- No execution without a reviewed plan for data-write or rules changes
