    25	- **Pause dates**, in `YYYY-MM-DD` strings:
    26	  - `scheduledPause.startDate` / `.endDate`;
    27	  - `pauseHistory[]` entries, which use **either** `startDate`/`endDate` **or** the legacy `start`/`end`.
    28	- **Last day:** `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
    29	- **`memberSince`:** added in Phase B (#36).
    30	
    31	`tinker-hq-apps` → `users/{uid}` (Tinker HQ staff): `role`, `appAccess[]`, `active`. Read by the link to build the staff roster.
    32	
    33	## The one-way link (#53)
    34	
    35	1. A 2nd-gen trigger in `tinker-hq-apps` (`clayhub-link`) fires when a `clayHub_members` doc changes. It collects the `memberId` from the before **and** after versions.
    36	2. For each `memberId`, it runs **one query filtered on `memberId` only**, and decides live/retired in memory. The query's `readTime` is the snapshot time.
    37	   - exactly one live doc → a snapshot of that doc's allowed fields;
    38	   - no live doc → a tombstone;
    39	   - **more than one live doc → a conflict:** nothing is sent, and it alerts.
    40	3. It POSTs the envelope (below) to the private HTTPS function `ingestMemberUpdate` in `my-clay-hub`, using its own service account's identity token. Only 200, 400 and 409 answers are final; anything else throws, so the trigger is retried.
    41	4. `ingestMemberUpdate`, in a transaction:
    42	   - rejects the payload unless it's strictly valid;
    43	   - **ignores it unless `readTime` is later than the stored `sourceReadTime`** (a member with no stored time accepts anything), comparing seconds *and* nanoseconds; an accepted envelope always advances `sourceReadTime`, even when nothing else changed;
    44	   - runs `deriveStatus`, and writes `members/{memberId}` and `memberProfiles/{memberId}` together;
    45	   - **never deletes**; a removal replaces the doc with a removed record (#71).
    46	
    47	- **Staff roster:** `users/{uid}` changes flow the same way into `staffRoster/staff_{uid}`, using that document read's `readTime`. Only people with an explicit grant are sent: `role` exactly `admin`|`manager`|`staff`, `active` absent or `true`, `appAccess` absent or a list of strings, and a manager or admin role or `appAccess` containing `my-clay-hub` (#68). Anything else, including a malformed doc, becomes a removal (malformed also alerts, naming the uid only); a removal for someone never held writes nothing.
    48	- **Reconcile:** every 6 hours (01:15, 07:15, 13:15, 19:15 UTC). It reads the whole source in **one read-only transaction pinned to a single `readTime`**, then sends the complete set in one `reconcile` envelope per scope; `ingestMemberUpdate` works out every change and applies it in **one transaction**, or nothing.
    49	  - If the read is incomplete, or a live member doc has no valid `memberId`, it sends nothing and alerts.
    50	  - A `memberId` with more than one live doc is sent as **held**: neither updated nor removed.
    51	  - A record newer than the batch (a trigger landed meanwhile) is never removed.
    52	  - The safety stops (#72) apply; a stop writes nothing, answers 409 and logs the counts and ids.
    53	- `sourceReadTime` is a `tinker-hq-apps` timestamp. It's only ever compared with other `tinker-hq-apps` read times.
    54	
    55	**Copied fields only** — rebuilt from allowed keys at every level, never copied and trimmed: `name`, `email` (strings, else `null`), `emailLower`, `memberSince` (a valid date, else `null`), `stage` (a known stage, else `"!malformed"`), `retired` (only `true`), `scheduledPause` (`null`, `{startDate, endDate, processed}`, or `"!malformed"`), `pauseHistory` (entries `{startDate, endDate, priorTerm?}`, legacy `start`/`end` mapped), `scheduledCancellation` (`null`, `{finalAccessDate}`, or `"!malformed"`), and **`phoneLast4`**, worked out in `tinker-hq-apps` with Membership Manager's own phone rule (10 digits, or 11 starting with 1; else `null`). Every date is a valid `YYYY-MM-DD`, absent, or `"!malformed"` — never raw text. `firstName` and `lastInitial` are worked out on receipt. The full phone number never leaves that project (#24).
    56	
    57	**Never copied, at any nesting level:** `keypadCode`, `keypadUserId`, `staffNotes`, `notes` (including the notes inside pause and cancellation entries), `application`, `actions`, the full phone, the shelf fields, billing and Sawyer fields (`lastBilling`, `processDate`, `sawyerProcessedAt`, …), audit timestamps (`scheduledAt` is reduced to the `processed` flag), and anything not listed above.
    58	
    59	**The envelope:** `{v:1, kind: 'member'|'staff'|'reconcile', readTime: {seconds: "<decimal string>", nanos: <int>}, …}` — the exact contract, fixtures and tests are in the Phase E plan (`my-clay-hub-phase-e-link`, "The link contract") and in the shared fixture set both repos test against. Logs never contain names, emails, phone digits, notes or source documents.
    60	
    61	## `deriveStatus(source, todayDenver)` (#34, #35)
    62	
    63	Code: `shared/derive-status.js`, using `shared/denver-time.js`. These are the only status and date code: `ingestMemberUpdate` and
    64	the daily recompute (09:30 UTC, #65) import them, and nothing re-derives status elsewhere. `todayDenver` is passed in, never read from the clock inside.
    65	
    66	Denver calendar dates only. `YYYY-MM-DD` strings are compared as dates, never through `new Date()`. A date must be strictly
    67	`YYYY-MM-DD` and a real day (no `2026-02-30`, no other shapes); anything else is **malformed**. The rules below run in order; the first match wins.
    68	
    69	1. No live source record (tombstone) → **`removed`**
    70	2. `stage` is `onboarding` or `touring` → **`not_yet`**
    71	3. `stage` is missing, or isn't one of the six known values → **`review`**
    72	4. `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate`:
    73	   - present but malformed → **`review`**;
    74	   - valid, and today is **after** it → **`offboarded`**. The last day itself still has access.
    75	5. `stage: 'cancelled'` with no `finalAccessDate` → **`offboarded`**
    76	6. `stage: 'offboarding'` with no `finalAccessDate` → **`review`**
    77	7. A `scheduledPause` that isn't an object is malformed → **`review`**. A `scheduledPause` object Membership Manager hasn't processed (`processed` isn't `true`) is **ignored** (#70; pause history entries are always processed).
    78	8. Any pause window (in a processed `scheduledPause` or any `pauseHistory` entry, either spelling) that is **missing, malformed, or reversed** (its end is before its start) → **`review`** (C8). A one-day pause (start = end) is valid. A pause with a start but **no end
    79	   date** is `review` too, never "paused indefinitely" (#59): staff see the flag and add the end date, and the pause's booking
    80	   cancellation happens then (a window with no end gives nothing to cancel against).
    81	9. Any valid pause window with **start ≤ today ≤ end** (both days included) → **`paused`**
    82	10. `stage: 'paused'` with no pause windows at all → **`review`**
    83	11. Otherwise → **`active`**. That covers `active`, a paused stage whose window has ended, `offboarding` before the last day, and `cancelled` with a future last day.
    84	
    85	How the code reads the edges of these rules (D-5):
    86	- Rule 1 also treats a record with `retired: true` as no live record, since live means `retired !== true`.
    87	- A cleared pause or cancellation is `null` in Membership Manager, and counts as absent. A `scheduledCancellation` without a
    88	  `finalAccessDate` (`null` or missing) means no last day. Any other `finalAccessDate`, **including an empty string**, must be a
    89	  valid date or it's malformed (rule 4 → `review`).
    90	- A pause entry uses `startDate`/`endDate` when they're set, else the legacy `start`/`end`.
    91	- A source that isn't a record at all gives `review`. `deriveStatus` never throws on member data; it throws only if `todayDenver`
    92	  itself isn't a valid date (a caller bug). Supported dates are 1900–2999.
    93	- **Input shape:** `deriveStatus` reads the `clayHub_members` field shape (`stage`, `scheduledPause`, `pauseHistory`,
    94	  `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate`). Whatever `members/*` stores, `ingestMemberUpdate` and the daily recompute must
    95	  hand it that shape. A flattened record would silently read as "no pause, no last day". Phase E tests that round trip.
    96	- **Deliberate differences from Membership Manager**, where it reads the same fields differently:
    97	  - A missing `stage` is `review` here (rule 3). Membership Manager treats it as active.
    98	  - Waitlisted and deferred people are stored as `stage: 'cancelled'`, so they derive to `offboarded`, not `not_yet`. Neither
    99	    can sign in, so the outcome is the same; it means `offboarded` isn't only former members.
   100	- As a check, run against the Sep 28, 2026 backup of all 66 `clayHub_members` records: every date was strict `YYYY-MM-DD`, and
   101	  none came out as `review`.
   102	
   103	| Status | Can sign in | Can book | Notes |
   104	|---|---|---|---|
   105	| `active` | yes | yes | |
   106	| `paused` | yes | no | Feed, What's on and My time are visible. The paused message names the day booking reopens (end + 1). |
   107	| `review` | yes | no | "We're checking your membership details — you can still see the feed." Staff see a flag. |
   108	| `offboarded`, `not_yet`, `removed` | no | no | `enforceMemberStatus` removes the claim, revokes sessions, and disables offboarded accounts (never deletes them). |
   109	
   110	It runs inside `ingestMemberUpdate` on every write, and again for everyone daily at **09:30 UTC** (#65), for that day's Denver date. The recompute is one transaction; it rewrites `status`, `statusDate` and the profile's `pause`, and stops on more unexplained changes than #72 allows.
   111	
   112	## Collections in `my-clay-hub`
   113	
   114	`members/{memberId}`: the projection. It's written **only** by `ingestMemberUpdate` and, for `status`/`statusDate` only, the daily recompute (both as `ingest@`, never deleting).
   115	- The copied fields above, plus `memberId`, `firstName`, `lastInitial`, `status`, `statusDate` (the Denver date it was derived for), `sourceReadTime`, `tombstone`, `updatedAt`.
   116	- **A removed member (#71)** keeps the last stored fields **minus `email`, `emailLower` and `phoneLast4`**, with `tombstone: true` and `status: 'removed'`.
   117	- **No client can read it**, not even the member themselves: Firestore rules can't hide single fields, and it holds `phoneLast4` (#24). Functions and rules read it on the server.
   118	
   119	`memberProfiles/{memberId}`: the **member-readable view**, written by `ingestMemberUpdate` alongside `members` (and its `status`/`pause` by the daily recompute). Exactly `memberId`, `firstName`, `name`, `email`, `status`, `memberSince`, `pause` (the valid, processed window containing today, else the earliest one starting after today, else `null`), `finalAccessDate` (only if valid), `updatedAt`. **Never `phoneLast4`, never a malformed marker.** A removed member's profile is just `{memberId, tombstone: true, status: 'removed', updatedAt}`. A member can read only their own (from Phase F; deny-all until then).
   120	
   121	`staffRoster/staff_{uid}`: `{ uid, name, role, sourceReadTime, updatedAt, tombstone }` for granted staff only (#68), written only by `ingestMemberUpdate`; a removal leaves `{ uid, tombstone: true, sourceReadTime, updatedAt }`. **No client can read it**; rules and functions check it.
   122	
   123	`linkOverrides/{id}`: single-use, scoped, expiring overrides for the safety stops (#72), created only by Christie in the Console. Exact keys per scope (`members`: `maxStatusChanges?`, `maxRemovals?`; `staff`: `maxRemovals`; `recompute`: `maxStatusChanges`), plus `scope`, `expiresAt` (≤ 24 h after the doc's creation) and `usedAt` (set when used). **Deny-all for every client, permanently.**
   124	
   125	`settings/app`: a single doc, editable by managers and admins (#50).
   126	- `areas`: `[{ id: 'glaze', name: 'Glaze station', capacity: 4 }, { id: 'wheels', name: 'Wheels', capacity: 10 }, { id: 'handbuilding', name: 'Handbuilding table', capacity: 6 }]`. The 10 wheels include the 2 standing wheels, which aren't a separate area (#8).
   127	- `openTime: '05:00'`; `closeTimes: { mon…sun: '23:00' }`. Tuesday is locked at 23:00; the others can be set to 24:00 later (#27).
   128	- `weeklyCapHours: 20`, where the week runs from Mon 00:00 to the next Mon 00:00, America/Denver (C6).
   129	- `bookAheadDays: 14` (#49)
   130	- `startStepMinutes: 15`; `lengthChipsHours: [1,2,3,4,5,6]`; `maxLengthHours: 6`; `endTimeStepMinutes: 15` (#48)
   131	- `earlyCheckoutRefund: { stepMinutes: 15, rounding: 'up' }` (#48)
   132	- `timing: { checkInOpensBeforeMin: 15, reminderMin: 10, lastCallMin: 20, releaseMin: 30, stillHereBeforeEndMin: 10 }`
   133	- `extensionOptionsMin: [30, 60, 90, 120]`
   134	- `kilns: [{ name: 'Hestia' }, { name: 'Lumi' }]`
   135	- `links: { askClayHub: 'https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd-RhLmSXsrlzow3JK7m0H77pEp3Gg5_zo0eKxNBBru1v0QoA/viewform', membershipEmail: 'clayhub@tinkerartstudio.com' }`
