   105	| `active` | yes | yes | |
   106	| `paused` | yes | no | Feed, What's on and My time are visible. The paused message names the day booking reopens (end + 1). |
   107	| `review` | yes | no | "We're checking your membership details — you can still see the feed." Staff see a flag. |
   108	| `offboarded`, `not_yet`, `removed` | no | no | `enforceMemberStatus` removes the claim, revokes sessions, and disables offboarded accounts (never deletes them). |
   109	
   110	It runs inside `ingestMemberUpdate` on every write, and again for everyone daily at **09:30 UTC** (#65), for that day's Denver date. The recompute is one transaction; it rewrites `status`, `statusDate` and the profile's `pause`, and stops on more unexplained changes than #72 allows.
   111	
   112	## Collections in `my-clay-hub`
   113	
   114	`members/{memberId}`: the projection. It's written **only** by `ingestMemberUpdate` and, for `status`/`statusDate` only, the daily recompute (both as `ingest@`, never deleting).
   115	- The copied fields above, plus `memberId`, `firstName`, `lastInitial`, `status`, `statusDate` (the Denver date it was derived for), `sourceReadTime`, `tombstone`, `updatedAt`.
   116	- **A removed member (#71)** keeps the last stored fields **minus `email`, `emailLower` and `phoneLast4`**, with `tombstone: true` and `status: 'removed'`.
   117	- **No client can read it**, not even the member themselves: Firestore rules can't hide single fields, and it holds `phoneLast4` (#24). Functions and rules read it on the server.
   118	
   119	`memberProfiles/{memberId}`: the **member-readable view**, written by `ingestMemberUpdate` alongside `members` (and its `status`/`pause` by the daily recompute). Exactly `memberId`, `firstName`, `name`, `email`, `status`, `memberSince`, `pause` (the valid, processed window containing today, else the earliest one starting after today, else `null`), `finalAccessDate` (only if valid), `updatedAt`. **Never `phoneLast4`, never a malformed marker.** A removed member's profile is just `{memberId, tombstone: true, status: 'removed', updatedAt}`. A member can read only their own (from Phase F; deny-all until then).
   120	
   121	`staffRoster/staff_{uid}`: `{ uid, name, role, sourceReadTime, updatedAt, tombstone }` for granted staff only (#68), written only by `ingestMemberUpdate`; a removal leaves `{ uid, tombstone: true, sourceReadTime, updatedAt }`. **No client can read it**; rules and functions check it.
   122	
   123	`linkOverrides/{id}`: single-use, scoped, expiring overrides for the safety stops (#72), created only by Christie in the Console. Exact keys per scope (`members`: `maxStatusChanges?`, `maxRemovals?`; `staff`: `maxRemovals`; `recompute`: `maxStatusChanges`), plus `scope`, `expiresAt` (≤ 24 h after the doc's creation) and `usedAt` (set when used). **Deny-all for every client, permanently.**
   124	
   125	`settings/app`: a single doc, editable by managers and admins (#50).
   197	## Server functions
   198	
   199	**In `tinker-hq-apps`** (codebase `clayhub-link`: read-only there, and it can only invoke `ingestMemberUpdate`):
   200	- `onClayHubMemberWritten`, `onStaffUserWritten`: re-read the source and send a snapshot.
   201	- `reconcileLink`: every 6 hours, as above.
   202	- Their two Cloud Run services' only invoker is `clayhub-link@` itself (#73).
   203	
   204	**In `my-clay-hub`:**
   205	- `ingestMemberUpdate`: private HTTPS; its only invoker is `clayhub-link@tinker-hq-apps`. The writer of `members`, `memberProfiles` and `staffRoster`. Runs `deriveStatus`. Can't delete.
   206	- `recomputeStatuses`: daily at 09:30 UTC (#65); one transaction; writes only `status`, `statusDate` and the profile's `status`/`pause`.
   207	- `claimMembership`: callable after sign-in. Uses the verified email only; exactly one live, sign-in-eligible member; sets `member: {memberId}` (#33).
   208	- `exchangeStaffSession`: verifies the Tinker HQ ID token, checks `staffRoster/staff_{uid}`, then getUser/createUser → claims → custom token (#31).
   209	- `enforceMemberStatus`: removes claims, revokes sessions, and disables accounts for `offboarded`, `not_yet` and `removed`.
   210	- `onMemberStatusChange`: a trigger on `members/{memberId}` in `my-clay-hub` that fires when `status` or a pause window changes.
   211	  - A new or changed pause window cancels that member's bookings inside the window.
   212	  - `offboarded` cancels all their future bookings.
   213	  - Each cancellation writes an inbox notice and an activity-log entry. It's idempotent.
   214	- `onBookingWrite`: validates the cap, maintains `weeklyHours` and `occupancy`, writes to `activityLog`.
   215	- `scheduledTicker` (or per-booking Cloud Tasks): reminder (+10), last call (+20, plus the staff no-show alert and push), release (+30), "Still here?" (end −10), auto check-out, the closing-time message, and event-day reminders. All idempotent.
   216	- `kioskLookup(last4)`: kiosk role only. Returns candidates `{ memberId, firstName, lastInitial, bookingNow? }` (#24).
   217	- `kioskNowList`: kiosk role only. The "Here now / Arriving soon" first-name list (#45).
   218	- `exportCsv(type, filters)`: staff with reports access only (#50).
   219	
   220	All scheduled jobs are 2nd gen, with explicit retries, run in America/Denver, and are tested for DST changes and week boundaries.

